      "id": 99531,
      "name": "boxwood",
      "username": "boxwood",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/eb8c5e/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-04-17T01:08:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Well it is pretty clear that the Egyptian relics have have had some physical effects on those who works them, take Shu, Geb, and several others as an example before raising that tomb that whole team were normal humans, now we have a ghost lady and a snake headed guy. So I guess I’m too dismissive I’d the Thiago theory, but whenever he’s used in a theory it just seems like an epileptic tree (he’s the operatives son, he is the new Ra, he takes up the legacy mantle one day although this one makes the most sense because of how he’s dressed in every appearance)</p>\n<p>As far as why I think Atum could be the new Ra, they do look rather similar to me, in Egyptian myth Atum and Ra sometimes are merged. And it just makes sense that someone tired to Ra’s storyline would take up his mantle, also shattered timelines set the precedent of a nemesis taking up their enemies mantle a (fright train becoming bunker)</p>\n<p>Although this could just be some new guy, or Guise, it’s probably just Guise being Guise.</p>",
